---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description={`Cookie Policy for ${site.companyName} (${site.brand}) — what cookies are, which ones this website uses, and how to manage them.`}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="legal">
        <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: 25 October 2026</p>

        <p>
          This Cookie Policy explains how <strong>{site.companyName}</strong> (&ldquo;{site.brand}&rdquo;,
          &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) uses cookies and similar technologies on{' '}
          <strong>{site.domain}</strong>. It should be read together with our{' '}
          <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files that are stored on your device when you visit a website. They help a
          website remember information about your visit, such as your preferences or whether you have visited
          before. &ldquo;Similar technologies&rdquo; include local storage and other browser-based mechanisms
          that serve comparable functions.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This website is primarily a static, business-to-business information site. It uses only a limited set
          of cookies and similar technologies, which fall into the following categories:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Strictly necessary / functional.</strong> These are required for the website to operate
            correctly, such as remembering basic session state or preferences. Without them, parts of the site
            may not function as expected.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics / performance.</strong> Where enabled, these help us understand aggregate usage —
            for example which pages are visited and how visitors move through the site — so we can improve the
            content and structure. This information is aggregated and is not used to identify you personally.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use cookies for targeted advertising on this website, and we do not sell data collected
          through cookies to third parties.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Some pages may use third-party services (for example, embedded maps, videos or analytics providers)
          that set their own cookies. These third parties may collect information in accordance with their own
          privacy and cookie policies. We encourage you to review those policies where such services appear.
        </p>

        <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Most web browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings. You can typically choose to
          block all cookies, block third-party cookies, or delete cookies that have already been set. Please
          note that disabling cookies may affect the functionality of this and other websites.
        </p>
        <p>
          For guidance on managing cookies in your browser, refer to the help documentation for your browser
          (for example Chrome, Safari, Firefox or Edge). You can also generally delete existing cookies through
          your browser&rsquo;s privacy or history settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of
          this page indicates when the current version took effect.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>If you have any questions about this Cookie Policy, please contact us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
          <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> {site.whatsapp}</li>
          <li><strong>Address:</strong> {site.address}</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Related documents: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> &middot; <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> &middot; <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
